@ 46.11 - Middle Chinese to Cantonese Vowel Shift (“The Inner-Outer Flip”)
# citation: LoneWolf, from Newman, J. (1983). Cahiers de Linguistique Asie Orentale XII.1:65 – 79. Relevant changes occurring before the shift: The actual vowel shift: Other relevant changes occurring at the same time: (Apparently, /i u/ either were or became glides in the appropriate positions)
	a > ɔ / _{ŋ,k}
	uə yə > ɔ œ / _{n,t}
	ə > ∅ / i_{ŋ,k}
	∅ > ə / C:[+labiovelar]_i
	∅ > ə / _u
	V > V:[+long] / _#
	ə > a
	a > {a:[+long],ə} “(the environments for these respective changes are somewhat unclear)”
	ə > a / _{i,u}
	iəu > au
	a > a:[+long] / _{i,u}
	a > ə / i_u
	ə > ∅ / i_u
	ə > ∅ / W_
	W > ∅ / C_